All changes are in. The game-over screen now presents an explicit choice instead of restarting on any input:

- **End screen buttons** — the game-over overlay keeps the score/hi-score/new-record display and now shows a neon-green "▶ PLAY AGAIN" button and a cyan "MAIN MENU" button, styled to match the arcade cabinet look.
- **Play Again** — calls the existing `startGame()`, which already rebuilds the snake, food, score, speed, and timers from scratch.
- **Main Menu** — a new `returnToMenu()` switches back to the title screen (with the INSERT COIN button and view-mode select) and wipes every piece of session state: snake, food, power-up, queued turns, particles, trail, slow-mo/ghost effects, screen shake, and score. It also repaints the canvas so the dead snake doesn't linger behind the menu, and plays a little descending beep.
- **Keyboard support** — on the game-over screen, Space/Enter plays again and M/Escape returns to the menu; a small hint line under the buttons documents both. The old "tap anywhere to continue" behavior was removed so a tap can't accidentally restart when the player meant to pick a button.

Edge cases handled: the render loop guards on `snake`/`food` being null, so the menu state renders cleanly in all three view modes; the power-up HUD badges hide automatically once the state leaves playing/paused; and Space on the game-over screen takes priority over its 3D "rise" binding.
